     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 10/7/14, 6:15 PM, Hadley Wickham\r\n      wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">Now that dplyr 0.3 is here, I&#39;d highly recommend\r\n      avoiding such shims and using the built in tools instead. Start\r\n      with the nse vignette. \r\n      <div><br>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <div>Hadley<br>\r\n        <br>\r\n        On Tuesday, October 7, 2014, Michael Cawthon &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mcaw...@greenstenergy.com</a>&gt;\r\n        wrote:<br>\r\n        <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n          <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"> You want this terrific\r\n            shim couresty of Sebastian Kranz:<br>\r\n            <br>\r\n            <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/skranz/9681509\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/skranz/9681509&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PSEPFtKP7VyhELhQAJrxd\">https://gist.github.com/skranz/9681509</a><br>\r\n            <br>\r\n            You might find the original SO Q&amp;A helpful as well: <br>\r\n            <br>\r\n            <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/21208801/group-by-multiple-columns-in-dplyr-using-string-vector-input\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/21208801/group-by-multiple-columns-in-dplyr-using-string-vector-input&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fcOcjyrxO2HyHvhkQzam9\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/21208801/group-by-multiple-columns-in-dplyr-using-string-vector-input</a><br>\r\n            <br>\r\n            <div>On 10/7/14, 5:26 PM, Stuart Luppescu wrote:<br>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n              <div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, I&#39;m trying to use dplyr to select cases\r\n                and variables from a data frame and am having trouble\r\n                when the name of the variable to select is held in\r\n                another variable. \r\n                <div><br>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div>I did this:</div>\r\n                <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><a href=\"http://meas.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://meas.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2e525xtTjllnAHHtUOcOvm\">meas.name</a> &lt;- as.character(<a href=\"http://as.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://as.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2VlesUivtBXnzx2pSu56Do\">as.name</a>(paste(themeas,\r\n                    &quot;_measure1&quot;, sep=&#39;&#39;)))<br>\r\n                    and then foo &lt;- df %&gt;% filter(target_num == 1)\r\n                    %&gt;% select(<a href=\"http://meas.name\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://meas.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2e525xtTjllnAHHtUOcOvm\">meas.name</a>)</font></blockquote>\r\n                <div>but I get this message:</div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                  <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Error in abs(ind[ind\r\n                      &lt; 0]) :  </font></blockquote>\r\n                  <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> non-numeric\r\n                      argument to mathematical function</font></blockquote>\r\n                </div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                  <div><br>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                  <div>Then I tried removing <font face=\"courier new,\r\n                      monospace\">as.character,</font><font face=\"arial,\r\n                      helvetica, sans-serif\"> but only got this:</font></div>\r\n                  <div>\r\n                    <blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\">Error in\r\n                      select_vars_(names(.data), dots) : <br>\r\n                        (list) object cannot be coerced to type &#39;double&#39;<br>\r\n                    </blockquote>\r\n                    <div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"><br>\r\n                    </div>\r\n                    <div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Can I\r\n                        get some help, please?</font></div>\r\n                    <div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I&#39;m\r\n                        using dplyr 0.3 with R 3.1.1</font></div>\r\n                    <div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">TIA</font></div>\r\n                    <div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">--</div>\r\n                  </div>\r\n                  Stuart Luppescu -- pixbuf .at. <a href=\"http://gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792357879360000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PenagNOxUewlWOaimh5o0\">gmail.com</a><br>\r\n                  What&#39;s another word for euphemism?<br>\r\n                    -- Karen Ellis: <a href=\"http://planetkaren.girl-wonder.org/index.php?strip_id=608\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.goog